  "description": "The canonical Stable Diffusion 1.x serve layout: the diffusers multifolder packaging (unet / vae / text_encoder), all-bf16. Derived from the real safetensors headers of stable-diffusion-v1-5/stable-diffusion-v1-5. Matching is per component file, so every family is optional and each file matches the families it carries. What separates this document from sd2.diffusers-bf16 is RANK, and it is a refusal rather than a shrug: SD1.x omits use_linear_projection, so every unet.*.attentions.{i}.proj_{in,out}.weight is a 1x1 Conv2d (rank 4) where SD2.x has a Linear (rank 2). The VAE mid-block attention keeps the pre-0.18 diffusers query/key/value/proj_attn spelling, which SD2.x checkpoints no longer carry. The clip_l.* role vocabulary uses the #q/#k/#v suffixes so the original single-file packaging's fused in_proj_weight converts to and from this one as a run-preserving derive. Top-level dtype is the serve-side load dtype (ctx.lane.dtype); the per-tensor dtypes are the matcher's constraint that this really is the bf16 packaging.",
